{"nodes": [{"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_covering_system", "label": "Covering-system characterization of obstructed primes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Obstruction (k=0) is a covering system in the sense of Erdos: propagation rule q|p-2^k and ord(2,q)|(m-k) => q|p-2^m poisons an AP of m-values; obstructed = these APs cover all valid m."}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_backbone", "label": "Backbone {3,5,7} with orders {2,4,3}, period 12", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_mod255255", "label": "Mod-255255 obstruction classifier (3.5.7.11.13.17)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_22_classes", "label": "22 unconditional obstruction classes mod 255255", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_subgroup_exclusion", "label": "Subgroup exclusion proof (3^n not in <3> mod blocking prime)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "3 is not a primitive root mod certain primes, so <3> is a proper subgroup of (Z/lZ)*; the forced residue of p-2^m falls outside <3>, contradicting p-2^m = 3^n. Blocking primes {13,37,41,61,67,73,181,193}, max 193."}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_k_distribution", "label": "k-distribution fit (negative binomial, overdispersed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "NegBin (Gamma-mixed Poisson) wins because it is a Poisson whose rate varies across primes = covering-class heterogeneity; mean 1.882, var 2.249, dispersion 1.19 (overdispersed)."}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_r_distribution", "label": "r-distribution (r = floor(log2 p) - k, misses per prime)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_magnitude_stationarity", "label": "Magnitude-stationarity of mean_k (~1.88, band-invariant)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The m available positions and the ~1/m per-position prime-power density cancel, so expected hit count is band-invariant; confirmed empirically flat across bands 2^30..2^39."}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_index_difference", "label": "Index-difference / S-unit relation on Mersenne factors", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For two representations 2^{m2}*M_d = q2^{n2}-q1^{n1}, d=m1-m2; primitive factors ell of M_d=2^d-1 (ord_ell(2)=d) give q2^{n2} = q1^{n1} mod ell, an S-unit relation keyed on d."}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_parity_lock", "label": "Index differences are parity-locked (all d even)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Within one prime every hit position m shares a common parity fixed by p mod 3 (ord_2(3)=2); enables storing the hit set as one int64 bitmask k-agnostically and dropping the d-vector."}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_ladic_power_residue", "label": "l-adic power-residue symbol analysis", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whether p-2^m is an n-th power decomposes into v_l divisible by n plus unit part being an n-th power in Z_l*; informative filtration primes are exponent-dependent (l with gcd(n,l-1)>1)."}, {"id": "markdown_math_lab_notes_burhanuddin_thesis", "label": "Burhanuddin thesis (2007) \u2014 l-adic BSD computations", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "markdown_math_lab_notes_backbone", "target": "markdown_math_lab_notes_covering_system", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "markdown_math_lab_notes_mod255255", "target": "markdown_math_lab_notes_covering_system", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "markdown_math_lab_notes_22_classes", "target": "markdown_math_lab_notes_mod255255", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "markdown_math_lab_notes_subgroup_exclusion", "target": "markdown_math_lab_notes_22_classes", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "markdown/math/lab-notes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "markdown_math_lab_notes_k_distribution", "targe